---- the addenda (A.4, A.5): an exorcism lifts curses only for the checker, so its block is ⍝
⍝ emitted in place. A vow is erased, unless it is hopeful and this is a --debug build: then
its measure runs and traps unless it is at least 0 and below the last one. Register 63's ⍝
⍝ block holds the ⍤⥀ waiting for its ⥀ (−1: none), the function being emitted (its checker
record), the measure on entry to it (−1: no hopeful ⍤ᚠ) and how many inputs it measures. ⍝
